quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  19,1,"Kaf, Ha, Ya, ‘Ayn, Sad."
  19,2,"(This is) an account of the mercy of your Lord upon His servant Zakariyya (Zachariah),"
  19,3,when he called upon his Lord (secretly) in a low voice.
  19,4,"He said: ‘My Lord! Indeed, my bones have become feeble, and my head has turned white with age, yet in supplicating You, my Lord, I have never been disappointed (or unblessed)."
  19,5,"Indeed, I fear (what) my relatives (will do) after me while my wife is barren. So grant me an heir from Your presence."
  19,6,"He should inherit from me and inherit from the House of Ya‘qub (Jacob), and make him, my Lord, well-pleasing (to You).’"
  19,7,"(The angel said:) ‘O Zakariyya (Zachariah)! Indeed, We give you the good news of a son whose name is Yahya (John). We have not given such a name to anyone before.’"
  19,8,He said: ‘My Lord! How shall I have a son when my wife is barren and I have already become extremely old?’
  19,9,"He (the angel) said: ‘‘So shall it be. Your Lord says: ‘It is easy for Me, just as I created you before when you were nothing.’’’"
  19,10,He said: ‘My Lord! Grant me a sign.’ He said: ‘Your sign is that you will not (be able to) speak to people for three full (days and) nights (though in sound health).’
  19,11,Then he came out to his people from his worshipping chamber and conveyed to them through signs that they should glorify (Allah) morning and evening.
